- The pack of parts: a LIBRARY, not a page.
-
- A class reaches `web.js` and `web.view.tree` by being named here, and that is
- all the editor needs of this module: the shelf offers the two parts, the second
- level of its panel offers the primitives, and both read the tree beside the
- bundle. Nothing is drawn, so there is nothing to configure and nothing to keep
- in step with the editor.
-
- BEFORE SHORTENING THE LIST: a third of the pack is here to serve the rich text
- and the dropdown alone, and they stay, because inside a block there is nothing
- else to lay out prose and a choice with. Cutting anything here empties the second
- level of the panel or the shelf itself, not a showcase — the showcase is gone,
- and what it proved is proved by the tests instead.
$bog_vmap_part $mol_view
	- The parts of this pack. Everything else below is mol itself, carried along
	- so that a page can be laid out and not only assembled.
	Calc $bog_vmap_part_calc
	Map $bog_vmap_part_map
	Cell $bog_vmap_part_cell
	Plot $bog_vmap_part_plot
	-
